{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Before the flock.</b> He would set the rods before the eyes of the flock, so that they would gaze with wonder at the act of the one setting them, and it would be imprinted upon their imagination at the time of conception — for the image formed by the imaginative faculty during pregnancy produces, in most cases, upon the offspring the likeness of the thing pictured."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:41.931645975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}